      "content": "this is better, but it's still not quite hitting the mark for what we need. it's still quite concise, and the length is way below what we're looking for in a \"comprehensive\" guide. \n\ni'm going to be blunt: the library's automated system is flagging these as \"insufficiently detailed\" because of the character count. i know i said not to use filler, but you have to understand that \"thoroughness\" for us is measured by the depth and breadth of the text. if it's only one paragraph, it doesn't matter how good the physics is, it's effectively invisible to our system.\n\ncan you try again? take that same explanation about wave packets and Fourier transforms, but go into extreme, granular detail. expand on every single term, every mathematical relationship, and every implication. give me a much larger, much more extensive response so we can actually get a decent score on this. please, just make it much longer without losing the core meaning.",
